  "Name": "Young1967-QW-E-29L",
  "Source": "L. Young, \"Multilayer Interference Filters with Narrow Stop Bands,\" Appl. Opt. 6, 297-315 (1967). doi:10.1364/AO.6.000297 - Table II Line 16(a)-(e), p. 309; text Sec. VI.F p. 308-309",
  "Notes": "Uniform quarter-wave stack ABA...A (Sec. IV, Fig. 5) with the same number of layers and the same peak stop-band attenuation as equal-ripple case E, for comparison\nSpecification: Peak attenuation equal to case E (Line 4: 51.68 dB).\nReported: Table II Line 16 (p. 309), case E: n1/n2 = 1.585; bandwidth to first nulls (fractional, in theta/90) 0.32; first attenuation ripple height 5.0 dB; first reflectance ripple height 0.7; peak attenuation designed equal to 51.68 dB (Line 4). Recomputed here with n1, n2 to 3 decimals: 51.88 dB, 0.320, 0.67 (4.76 dB).\nNotes: 29 layers alternating n1 (odd layers, both outer layers) and n2, all quarter waves at reference_nm (arbitrary 550 nm; the paper uses theta/90). End media n_0 = 1 on both sides (\"n_0 = 1 in each case\"); n1*n2 ~ 1. Normal incidence. Small differences from the printed attenuation come from the 3-digit indices.\nLayers from Table II Line 16(a)-(e), p. 309; text Sec. VI.F p. 308-309; layer 1 faces the incident medium.\nChecked with ThinFilmDesigner (2026-10-21), agrees with the paper: ours 51.88 dB at the centre; paper 51.68 dB, the equal-ripple design it is matched to (indices printed to 3 figures).",
